# WarpX Compilation Instructions

## Environment Setup

Before compiling WarpX, always source the appropriate profile (CPU version):

```bash
source ~/cardinal_cpu_warpx.profile
```

## Basic Compilation

To compile WarpX, use CMake with the following basic command structure:

```bash
cmake -S . -B build -DWarpX_DIMS="2"
cmake --build build -j 8
```

The compiled binaries will be available in `build/bin/`.

## Important Notes

- **Dependencies are already installed** - Do NOT attempt to reinstall dependencies
- The dimensionality can be changed using `-DWarpX_DIMS` option (values: "1", "2", "3", "RZ", "RCYLINDER", "RSPHERE", or combinations like "1;2;3;RZ;RCYLINDER;RSPHERE")
- Common CMake options and build configurations are documented in [Docs/source/install/cmake.rst](mdc:Docs/source/install/cmake.rst)

## Common CMake Options

Refer to [cmake.rst](mdc:Docs/source/install/cmake.rst) for detailed options, including:
- `WarpX_COMPUTE`: Backend selection (NOACC/OMP/CUDA/SYCL/HIP)
- `WarpX_DIMS`: Simulation dimensionality
- `WarpX_MPI`: Multi-node support
- `WarpX_OPENPMD`: openPMD I/O support
- `WarpX_PRECISION`: Floating point precision
- `WarpX_QED`: QED support
- `WarpX_FFT`: FFT-based solvers

## Build Directory

The existing build directory is `build_cardinal_cpu/` which contains pre-built binaries for multiple dimensions (1d, 2d, 3d, rz).
